From: Lu-Fi <lutz@fiebach.de>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 14:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] motor-daemon: flip the logical frame with the streamer image
 flips

A camera mounted upside-down is normally compensated in the streamer
(vflip+hflip on the image), so the picture on screen is upright but the
motor axes read backwards relative to that picture: pressing "up" moves
the view down, "right" moves it left. invert_x/invert_y can patch each
axis by hand, but the mount is already described by the flips - asking
the user to also know the motor wiring to set two more booleans is the
kind of cross-product of options nobody gets right.

XOR the streamer image flips into motor_inversion_state right after the
config invert_x/invert_y, so the logical frame is defined by what is on
screen:

  net_x = invert_x XOR hflip
  net_y = invert_y XOR vflip

Read from the streamer config (/etc/prudynt.json, image.vflip /
image.hflip - same key names as the agent-adapter exposes in the web
UI). Missing file / image object / keys mean "no flips". Because the XOR
sits next to the invert_x/invert_y XORs in load_config_file(),
everything downstream (motor_steps_impl, the absolute-move mirroring,
home mirroring, status replies) picks the net state up uniformly, and
R reloads pick up flip changes without a reboot.
---
--- a/src/motor-daemon.c
+++ b/src/motor-daemon.c
@@ -420,6 +420,30 @@ static bool parse_legacy_layout(JsonValue *root) {
   return parsed;
 }
 
+// Mirror the streamer's image flips into the inversion state so the
+// logical frame matches what is on screen:
+//   net_x = invert_x XOR hflip, net_y = invert_y XOR vflip
+static void apply_flip_inversion(void) {
+  JsonValue *root = parse_json_file("/etc/prudynt.json");
+  if (!root)
+    return;
+  if (root->type != JSON_OBJECT) {
+    free_json_value(root);
+    return;
+  }
+
+  JsonValue *image = get_object_item(root, "image");
+  if (image && image->type == JSON_OBJECT) {
+    bool hflip = false, vflip = false;
+    if (json_get_bool_jct(image, "hflip", &hflip) && hflip)
+      motor_inversion_state ^= MOTOR_INVERT_X;
+    if (json_get_bool_jct(image, "vflip", &vflip) && vflip)
+      motor_inversion_state ^= MOTOR_INVERT_Y;
+  }
+
+  free_json_value(root);
+}
+
 static void load_config_file(void) {
   JsonValue *root = parse_json_file("/etc/thingino.json");
   reset_config_defaults();
@@ -442,6 +466,8 @@ static void load_config_file(void) {
   if (!parsed)
     parsed = parse_legacy_layout(root);
 
+  apply_flip_inversion();
+
   if (parsed) {
     sanitize_axis_cfg(&g_cfg.pan);
     sanitize_axis_cfg(&g_cfg.tilt);
